      ]
    },
    {
      "image": "videos/18-thought-to-text/G5.jpg",
      "images": [
        "videos/18-thought-to-text/G6.jpg"
      ],
      "imageAt": [
        0,
        0.4
      ],
      "seconds": 18.63,
      "text": "For years the assumption was that silence meant the message was gone. It was not. The letter was written every time. The post office had closed. What these systems do is reopen it, and what they decode is the attempt to speak, not private thought. That distinction matters more every year, because it is the line everything built after this will be measured against.",
